According to an article here (and also in Caf-News on Feb 20, 1994),
three of the newsgroups were banned at Waterloo not on the advice of
legal counsel, but on the advice of an anti-porn "ethics" committee
that at the time didn't even have a librarian on it. Here is
the abstract from CAF-News:

UW censorship - where does it end?  Is Gopher to be censored?                  
    [paraphrase: The U. of Waterloo Ethics Committee banned alt.tasteless,     
    alt.sex.stories, and alt.sex.stories.d even though the university          
    legal counsel did NOT recommend removal of these newsgroup. 'The           
    Committee apparently decided on these ban because it felt that these       
    three groups "may from time to time contain `obscene' material".']         
    <CLHAGB.3nt@watserv1.uwaterloo.ca>              

If U. of Victoria wants to emulate U. of Waterloo, it should emulate
their decision to restore rec.humor.funny. And it should not think
that emulating U. of Waterloo is a substitute for getting competent
legal advice.

- Carl
